# Guards a manual `vercel deploy` from a checkout against the CLI source-upload caps (100 MB and
# 15,000 files). It also applies to Vercel Git builds (the ignored folders are absent from the
# build), so nothing the build imports or type-checks may live in an ignored folder: build-included
# code never imports from tests/ (tests/vercel-config.test.ts enforces it). It has no effect on
# `vercel deploy --prebuilt` (which uploads .vercel/output, not the source).
# The build needs data/, public/, scripts/, src/, messages/, content/, package.json and
# pnpm-lock.yaml: never list them here (tests/vercel-config.test.ts enforces it).
data-staging/
docs/
tests/
.claude/
.impeccable/
.superpowers/
test-results/
playwright-report/
node_modules/
.next/
.git/
